hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5476","The Magians were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: They let their moustaches grow long and shave their beards, so you do the opposite of them. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to trim his moustache in such a way as the hair of a goat or a camel is trimmed."
"5477","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever does not trim his mustache, he is not from one of us.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 13)"
"5478","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Trimming the moustache, cutting the nails, and removing the pubic hair are part of the natural disposition (fitrah)."
"5479","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Five things are part of natural disposition: trimming the moustache, removing the hair from the armpits, cutting the nails, removing the hair below the navel, and circumcision.\"""""
"5480","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""There are five acts of natural disposition: circumcision, removing the pubic hair, trimming the moustache, cutting the nails, and removing the hair from the armpits.\"""""
"5481","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""There are five acts of natural disposition: trimming the nails, shortening the moustache, removing the hair below the navel, circumcision, and removing the hair of the armpits.\"""""
"5482","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: The inborn characteristics of man are five. Another version says: Five things are of the inborn characteristics of man: circumcision, shaving the pubes, plucking out hair under the armpit, paring the nails and clipping the moustaches. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4198)"
"5483","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid visit to us, and saw a dishevelled man whose hair was disordered. He said: Could this man not find something to make his hair lie down? He saw another man wearing dirty clothes and said: Could this man not find something to wash his garments with. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4062)"
"5484","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combing (the hair) daily, but it can be done with a day's interval."
"5485","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to comb his hair backward, while the polytheists used to part their hair. The People of the Book"
"5486","The Messenger of Allah [SAW] used to tell his wives not to wear jewelry and silk. He said: ""If you want the jewelry and silk of Paradise, then do not wear them in this world."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5136)"
"5487","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold rings.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3643)"
"5488","A man came to the Prophet [SAW] and he was wearing an iron ring. He said: ""Why do I see you wearing the jewelry of the people of Hell?"" He threw it away, then he came and he was wearing a brass ring. He said: ""Why do I notice the stench of idols from you?"" So he threw it away, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what should I use?"" He said: ""Silver, but it should not equal a Mithqal."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5195)"
"5489","I have brought many embers with me. The man had brought several pieces of jewelry from Bahrain. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: You have not brought anything without which we cannot manage, however, this is merely the provision of worldly life. The man said: Please accept my apology. Let your companions not think that you are angry with me for any other reason. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) stood up, announced that he had accepted his apology, and clarified that his displeasure was only because of his ring."
"5490","I saw one day on the finger of Messenger of Allah (may peace be Upon him) a silver ring; so the people also got silver rings made and wore them Then Allah's Apostle ﷺ discarded his ring, and the people also discarded their rings. (Using translation from Muslim 2093a)"
"5491","""The Messenger of Allah [SAW] started to wear a gold ring, and the people started to wear gold rings. The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'I was wearing this ring, but I will never wear it again.' He threw it away and the people threw their rings away.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5164)"
"5492","I will never wear it again."
"5493","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had a ring made and he wore it, then he said: Today, this has distracted me from you. Then he took it off."
"5494","I will never wear it again."" Then he had a ring made of silver. He used to keep its stone towards the palm of his hand. He had the words ""Muhammad Rasul Allah"" engraved on it. This ring remained on his blessed hand until he passed away."
"5495","The Messenger of Allah [SAW] put on a ring of gold and he used to wear its stone (Fass) next to his palm. Then the people started to wear rings too. Then the Messenger of Allah [SAW] threw it away and said: ""I will never wear it again."" Then the Messenger of Allah [SAW] took a ring of silver, and wore it on his hand. Then it was on the hand of Abu Bakr, then on the hand of 'Umar, then on the hand of 'Uthman, until it was lost in the well of Aris. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5293)"
"5496","""The inscription on the ring of the Prophet ﷺ was in three lines: 'Muhammad' on a line, 'Messenger' on a line, and 'Allah' on a line."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1747)"
"5497","I have had a ring made. No one should engrave an inscription like its inscription."
"5498","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a ring made for him, and he said: ‘I have had a ring made for me and had it engraved, and no one should make a ring with similar engraving.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3640)"
"5499","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had a ring made of gold. He wore it on his right hand. He would keep the stone of the ring facing towards the palm. Then he removed it and had a ring made of silver."
"5500","The Messenger of Allah [SAW] put on a ring of gold, and he used to wear its stone (Fass) next to his palm. Then the people started to wear rings of gold. Then the Messenger of Allah [SAW] discarded it, and the people discarded their rings. Then he acquired a ring of silver with which he used to seal letters, but he did not wear it. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5218)"
"5501","""And Abu Salamah informed me"" - That the Prophet [SAW] used to wear his ring on his right hand. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5203)"
"5502","""I heard 'Ali say: 'The Prophet of Allah [SAW] forbade me to wear a ring on the forefinger and middle finger.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5286)"
"5503","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""The evil eye is a fact,"" and he forbade tattooing. (Using translation from Bukhārī 5944)"
"5504","The woman who tattoos and the one who gets tattooed, the one who plucks hair and the one who gets hair plucked, are cursed. Whereas I have read the entire Qur'an. I did not find in it what you state. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You would have found it, but you do not have knowledge. She asked: What is that? Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Have you not read this verse: ""Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you from, abstain from it."" The woman replied: Yes. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This is what is meant. The woman said: I think one of your noble wives also does such a thing. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Go inside the house and see her. The woman went inside the house. She examined, but did not find anything like that. Sayyiduna Abdullah asked the woman: Did you see anything like that? She replied: No. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If you had seen any such thing, then (i.e. a wife who did such a thing) would not have remained with me."
"5505","What is this news that has reached me from you that you curse those women who tattooed and those women who have themselves tattooed, the women who pluck hair from their faces and who make spaces between their teeth for beautification changing what God has created? Thereupon 'Abdullah said: Should I not curse one upon whom Messenger of Allah ﷺ has invoked curse and that is in the Book also. Thereupon that woman said: I read the Qur'an from cover to cover, but I did not find that in it. whereupon he said: If you had read (thoroughly) you would have definitely found this in that (as) Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, has said:"" What Messenger of Allah brings for you accept that and what he has forbidden you, refrain from that."" That woman said: I find this thing in your wife even now. Thereupon he said: Go and see her. She reported: I went to the wife of 'Abdullah but found nothing of this sort in her. She came back to him and said: I have not seen anything. whereupon he said: Had there been anything like it in her, I would have never slept with her in the bed. (Using translation from Muslim 2125a)"
"5506","The narrator says: I asked what is meant by qaza‘, so the narrator named Ubaidullah explained: When a child's head is shaved and some hair is left here and some hair is left there. The narrator named Ubaidullah pointed to his forehead and one side of his head while saying this. It was asked from Ubaidullah whether the ruling is the same for both girls and boys regarding this. He replied: I do not know. He (i.e., my teacher) narrated this hadith in this way."
"5507","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade qaza‘. (The narrator says:) What is meant by this is: the head is shaved and some hair is left."
"5508","The Prophet ﷺ saw a boy with part of his head shaved and part left unshaven. He forbade them to do that, saying: Shave it all or leave it all. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4195)"
"5509","By Allah, I am certain that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that. (Using translation from Aḥmad 101)"
"5510","narrations, the word ""zawr"" (meaning deception) is used, but the correct pronunciation is ""zawr,"" which can be read with either a kasrah or a dammah."
"5511","Mu'awiya came to Medina and he addressed us and he took out a bunch of hair and said: What do I see that one of you does but that what the Jews did? (I can well recall) that when this act (adding of artificial hair) reached Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he named it as cheating. (Using translation from Muslim 2127c)"
"5512","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: The Children of Israel were destroyed when their women began to use this."
"5513","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the woman who adds some false hair and the woman who asks for it, the woman who tattoos and the woman who asks for it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4168)"
"5514","narrates: A girl got married. She fell ill. Her hair fell out. Her family intended to attach artificial hair to her. They mentioned this matter to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has cursed the one who attaches artificial hair, the one who has artificial hair attached, and the one for whom artificial hair is attached."
"5515","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade a woman from attaching artificial hair to her head."
"5523","narrates about the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): When he would lie down to sleep, he would place his blessed right hand under his blessed right cheek and would recite this supplication: “O Allah! Save me from Your punishment on the Day when You will resurrect Your servants.”"
"5524","Fāṭimah came to the Prophet ﷺ to complain about the marks on her hands from grinding flour. She heard that the Prophet ﷺ had received some captives, so she went to him to request a servant but did not find him. Instead, she met ʿĀʾishah and shared her request with her. When the Prophet ﷺ returned, ʿĀʾishah informed him about Fāṭimah's request."",""So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us"",""and we had already taken our places in bed. We got up to greet him"","" and he said"","" """"Stay in your places."""" He then sat among us until I felt the coolness of his feet on my chest. He then said"","" """"I shall guide you to something better than having a servant: When you go to bed"","" say Allāhu akbar (Allah is the Greatest) thirty-four times"","" al-ḥamdu lillāh (Praise be to Allah) thirty-three times"","" and subḥān Allāh (Glory be to Allah) thirty-three times; This is better for you than having a servant."""""""
"5525","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Recite Surah Al-Kafirun."
"5526","I have left her with her mother."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""Then for what purpose have you come?"" He replied, ""I have come so that you may teach me something which I can recite at the time of sleeping."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""You should recite Surah Al-Kafirun and sleep with its concluding words; this Surah is a declaration of being free from shirk."
"5527","When you go to bed during night, you should say:"" O Allah, I surrender myself to Thee and entrust my affair to Thee, with hope in Thee and fear of Thee. There is no resort and no deliverer (from hardship but Thou). I affirm my faith in the Book which Thou revealed and in the Messengers whom Thou sent."" If you die in this state you would die on Fitra, and Ibn Bashshdr did not make a mention of"" night"" in this hadith. (Using translation from Muslim 2710c)"
"5528","from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: *""Whoever says when he retires to his bed:*"",""*(There is no god but Allah alone"",""with no partner. To Him belongs dominion"","" and to Him belongs praise"","" and He has power over all things. There is no might and no power except through Allah. Glory be to Allah"","" praise be to Allah"","" there is no god but Allah"","" and Allah is greatest)*"",""*Allah will forgive his sins or his misdeeds""""*"",""Misar was uncertain"","" *""""even if they are like the foam of the sea.""""*"""
"5529","I not guide you (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) or shall I not teach you something that is better for you than that? When you go to your bed (to sleep), recite Subhan Allah, Allahu Akbar, and La ilaha illallah thirty-three times each. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Since I heard this from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), I have never abandoned this practice. People asked: Not even on the night of the Battle of Siffin? He replied: Not even on the night of the Battle of Siffin (did I abandon this practice)."
"5530","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would wake up at night, he would recite this: ""There is no deity except Allah, He is One, He is Dominant, He is the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them. He is the Dominant and the Forgiving."
"5531","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ awake at night, he said: There is no god but thou, glory be to Thee, O Allah, I ask Thy pardon for my sin and I ask Thee for Thy mercy. O Allah! advance me in knowledge: do not cause my heart to deviate (from guidance) after Thou hast guided me, and grant me mercy from thyself; verily thou art the grantor. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5061)"
"5532","when the prophet (May peace be upon him) lay down on his bed (at night), he would say: O Allah! In Thy name I die and live. When he awoke, he said: praise be to Allah who has given us life after causing us to die and to whom we shall be resurrected. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5049)"
"5533","The angel says: End (the day's deeds) with goodness. The devil says: End (the day's deeds) with evil."" (The Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, says:) If that person sleeps while remembering Allah, the angels continue to protect him throughout the night. When he wakes up, the angel says: Begin (the day's deeds) with goodness, and the devil says: Begin with evil. If that person recites this: 'All praise is due to Allah who returned my soul to me and did not cause me to die during my sleep. All praise is due to Allah who has restrained the heavens and the earth from perishing. (He should recite this verse to the end.) All praise is due to Him who has restrained the sky from falling upon the earth except by His permission.'"
"5534","When any one of you goes to bed, he should take hold of the hem of his lower garment and then should clean (his bed) with the help of that and then should recite the name of Allah for he himself does tiot know what he left behind him on his bed, and when he intends to lie on bed, he should lie on his right side and utter these words:"" Hallowed be Allah, my Lord. It is with Thine (grace) that I place my side (upon the bed) and it is with Thee that I take it up (after sleep), and in case Thou withholdst my being (if thou causest me to die), then grant pardon to my being, and if Thou keepst (this process of breathing on), then protect it with that with which Thou protected Thine pious servants."" (Using translation from Muslim 2714a)"
"5535","I lay down my side (on the bed), and with Your help I will raise it up: O Allah! If You take my soul, then have mercy on it, and if You release it, then protect it with that which You protect Your righteous servants.'"" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Sa'id Maqburi heard this narration from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he also heard this narration from his father, who narrated it from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him). Both chains are preserved."
"5536","The Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) said to me: When you go to your bed, perform ablution like the ablution for prayer, and then lie on your right side and say: O Allah I have handed over my face to thee, entrusted my affairs to thee, and committed my back to thee out of desire for and fear to thee. There is no refuge and no place of safety from thee except by having recource to thee. I believe in Thy Book which Thou hast sent down and in Thy prophet whom thou hast sent down. He said : If you die (that night), you would die in the true religion, and utter these words in the last of that you utter (other prayers). Al-Bara said : I said: I memorise them, and then I repeated, saying “and in Thy Apostle whom Thou hast sent”. He said : No, say : “and in Thy Prophet whom Thou hast sent. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5046)"
"5537","When any one of you intends to go to sleep, he should lie on the bed on his right side and then say:"" O Allah. the Lord of the Heavens and the Lord of the Earth and Lord of the Magnificent Throne, our Lord, and the Lord of evervthina, the Splitter of the grain of corn and the datestone (or fruit kernal), the Revealer of Torah and Injil (Bible) and Criterion (the Holy Qur'an), I seek refuge in Thee from the evil of every- thing Thou art to sieze by the forelock (Thou hast perfect control over it). O Allah, Thou art the First, there is naught before Thee, and Thou art the Last and there is naught after Thee, and Thou art Evident and there is nothing above Thee, and Thou art Innermost and there is nothing beyond Thee. Remove the burden of debt from us and relieve us from want."" Abu Salih used to narrate it from Abu Huraira who narrated it from Allah's Apostle ﷺ. (Using translation from Muslim 2713a)"
"5538","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to his bed, he would say: Praise be to Allah Who has given me sufficiency, has guarded me, given me food and drink, been most gracious to me, and given to me most lavishly. Praise be to Allah in every circumstance. O Allah! Lord and King of everything, God of everything, I seek refuge in Thee from Hell. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5058)"
"5539","When the Prophet ﷺ went to bed, he used to say, ""Allahumma bismika ahya wa amut."" And when he woke up in the mornings he used to say, ""Al-hamdu li l-lahi al-ladhi ahyana ba'da ma amatana wa ilaihi-nnushur."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 7394)"
"5540","When the Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) went to his bed, he would say: Praise be to Allah who has fed us, given us drink, satisfied us and given us refuge. Many there are who have no one to provide sufficiency for them, or give them refuge. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5053)"
"5541","The narrator states: We think that he attributed this to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"5542","I have submitted myself to You. I have turned my face towards You. I have entrusted my affair to You. With desire and fear, there is no refuge and no escape from You except to You."
"5543","I have also seen Ibn Shihab Zuhri doing this."
"5544","Every night when he prophet (May peace be upon him) went to his bed, he joined his hands and breathed into them, reciting into them:”say: he is Allah, One” and say ; I seek refuge in the Lord of the dawn and Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of men. Then he would wipe as much of his body as he could with his hands, beginning with his head, his face and the front of his body, doing that three times. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5056)"
"5545","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Recite Surah Al-Kafirun."
"5546","I have left her with her mother."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""Then why have you come?"" He said, ""I have come so that you may teach me something which I can recite at night."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Recite Surah Al-Kafirun and after reciting it, go to sleep. This Surah is a declaration of freedom from shirk (polytheism)."
"5547","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would not sleep before the Isha prayer, nor would he engage in conversation after it."
"5548","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sleeping before the night prayer and talking after it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4849)"
"5549","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a man who was lying on his stomach (face down). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) nudged him with his foot and said: This is a way of lying down which Allah Almighty does not like."
"5550","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us after Maghrib while we were present at the platform of Suffah. He said: O so"
"5551","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""No person should lie on his back in such a way that one of his feet is placed over the other.\""(Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The act which the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade refers to a person lying on his back in such a way that one foot is placed over the other. The reason for this is that people used to wear waistcloths, and if"
"5552","'Abbad b. Tamim reported from his uncle that he saw Messenger of Allah ﷺ lying in the mosque and placing his one foot upon the other. (Using translation from Muslim 2100a)"
"5553","Jabir reported that Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the wrapping of oneself completely leaving no room for the arm and supporting oneself when sitting with a single garment wrapped round one's knees and a person raising one of his feet and placing it on the other while lying on his back. (Using translation from Muslim 2099c)"
"5554","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports this about the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): He forbade a man from lying on his back in such a way that he placed one of his feet over the other."
"5555","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Allah has forbidden for you, (1) to be undutiful to your mothers, (2) to bury your daughters alive, (3) to not to pay the rights of the others (e.g. charity, etc.) and (4) to beg of men (begging). And Allah has hated for you (1) vain, useless talk, or that you talk too much about others, (2) to ask too many questions, (in disputed religious matters) and (3) to waste the wealth (by extravagance)."
"5556","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbidding the burying of daughters alive, disobedience to mothers, not fulfilling the rights of others and usurping their rights, useless arguments and excessive questioning (i.e., unnecessary questions or asking without need), and wasting wealth. Imam Sha’bi narrated this report from Warad on the authority of Sayyiduna Mughirah (may Allah be pleased with him). This was stated by the Shaykh."
"5557","from the Prophet ﷺ [who] said, ""Verily, the most beloved of you and closest to me in the Hereafter are those with the best character. The most hateful of you to me and furthest from me in the Hereafter are those with the worst character: the braggarts, the verbose, the loquacious."""
"5558","""There are four whom Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, hates: The vendor who sells his wares by means of false oaths, the poor man who shows off, the old man who commits Zina and the Imam who is unjust."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2576)"
"5559","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deceives us (or commits fraud) is not from among us. Deceit and fraud will be in the Hellfire."
"5560","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever deceives a servant regarding his wife is not from among us, and whoever incites a woman against her husband is not from among us."
"5561","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Refrain from seven (characteristics) which cause destruction. He was asked: What are they, Messenger of Allah ? He replied: To assign partner to Allah, magic, to kill a soul (man) which is prohibited by Allah except for which is due, to take usury, to consume the property of an orphan, to retreat on the day of the battle, and to slander chaste women, indiscreet but believing. Abu Dawud said: The name Abu al-Ghaith is Salim client of Ibn Muti'. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2874)"
"5562","A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! What are the biggest sins?: The Prophet ﷺ said, ""To join others in worship with Allah."" The bedouin said, ""What is next?"" The Prophet ﷺ said, ""To be undutiful to one's parents."" The bedouin said ""What is next?"" The Prophet ﷺ said ""To take an oath 'Al-Ghamus."" The bedouin said, ""What is an oath 'Al-Ghamus'?"" The Prophet ﷺ said, ""The false oath through which one deprives a Muslim of his property (unjustly). (Using translation from Bukhārī 6920)"
"5563","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the major sins are associating partners with Allah, disobeying parents, and taking a false oath. By the One in Whose hand is my soul! If a person swears an oath about anything, even as small as a mosquito's wing, then on the Day of Resurrection that oath will be a burden (or a stain) upon his heart."
"5564","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr! I consider you weak. I like for you what I like for myself. Never become the guardian of an orphan’s wealth, and do not become the leader of even two people."
"5565","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say this from the pulpit: ""I urge you to be cautious regarding the wealth of two weak ones—the orphan and the woman."
"5566","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Have you not reflected? Allah Almighty has said: 'Indeed, those who consume the wealth of orphans unjustly are only filling their bellies with fire.'"
"5567","narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Ka’b bin ‘Ujrah! Such flesh and blood will not enter Paradise whose nourishment has been from the unlawful; the Fire is more deserving of them. O Ka’b bin ‘Ujrah! People go out in two conditions. One person frees himself and liberates himself, and another enslaves himself. O Ka’b bin ‘Ujrah! Prayer is a means of attaining closeness, charity is a proof, fasting is a shield, and charity wipes out sin just as a strong person climbs Safa.”"
"5568","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: ‘O ‘Aishah, beware of (evil) deeds that are regarded as insignificant, for they have a pursuer from Allah. (i.e. accountability).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4243)"
"5569","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Make a barrier between yourself and the unlawful by means of the lawful. Whoever does so will safeguard his honor and religion, and whoever grazes (his flock) near the sanctuary will soon be grazing within it. Every king has a sanctuary, and indeed, the sanctuary of Allah on earth is His prohibited things.”"
"5570","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: O Ali! You have a treasure and you are the one with two horns. Do not rais"
"5571","Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) about an accidental glance, so he instructed me to turn my gaze away.(Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The command to turn the gaze away is obligatory regarding that which is not permissible, and this is combined with the prohibition of its opposite, and that is, it is forbidden to look at that which has been declared unlawful."""
"5572","“The Prophet saw a woman, then he went to Zainab to fulfill his need and he left. He said: ‘Indeed when the woman enters, she enters in the image of Shaitan. So when one of you sees a woman that he is fascinated with, then let him go to his wife, for indeed with her (his wife) is the same as that which is with her.” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1158)"
"5573","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person sees a woman who pleases him, he should go to his wife and be intimate with her, for she has the same (pleasure and closeness)."
"5574","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A man is not to look at the 'Awrah of a man, and a woman is not to look at the 'Awrah of a woman. A man is not to be alone with a man under one garment, and a woman is not to be alone with a woman under one garment.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2793)"
"5575","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Both of you get up. We said: He is blind, he cannot see us. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Are both of you blind? Will you not see him? (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) ""Are you blind?"" Here, literally, information is being sought, but through this, what is meant is to prohibit both women from looking at that man who is blind. In this is evidence that it is also forbidden for women to look at men, except for mahram men, whose ruling is different. And this prohibition is equal, whether those men are blind or sighted."
"5576","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Both of you observe hijab from him. Both of them said, \""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Is he not blind? He cannot see us nor recognize us.\"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: \""Are you both not seeing him?\"""""
"5577","Utbah bin Abu Hakim narrates: He asked Sulaiman bin Musa about a person who looks at his wife's private part, so Sulaiman replied, ""I asked Ata about this, and he said, 'I asked Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) about this.' So Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said, 'The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and I used to perform ghusl from the same vessel, in which our hands would enter one after the other.'"
"5578","I came and informed the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) about this: Those people have left, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came until he entered the house. When I was about to enter, he hung a curtain between me and himself. Allah Almighty (on this occasion) revealed this verse: ""O you who believe! Do not enter the houses of the Prophet until permission is given to you."" This verse continues up to: ""Indeed, this is great in the sight of Allah."
"5579","I brought some people. They ate the food, then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and went outside. He came to the house of Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and I also followed him. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the house and found two men inside. When he saw them, he turned back and did not speak to them. Both of them got up and left the house. On this occasion, the verse regarding the command of hijab was revealed: ""O you who believe! Do not enter the houses of the Prophet until permission is given to you for food, and you are not looking towards the utensils."
"5580","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) never shook hands with any woman."
"5581","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would take (the pledge of allegiance) from women only for that thing which Allah Almighty had commanded him. The blessed hand of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) never touched the hand of any woman. When he would take the pledge from those women, he would say to them: I have taken your pledge by words."
"5582","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates as a marfu’ hadith that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “No man should have intercourse with another man, and no woman should have intercourse with another woman.”"""
"5583","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""No woman should press her body against another woman, nor should any man press his body against another man, except that a father may press his body against his child."
"5584","The narrator named Abu Salih is Mizan. He is from the people of Basra and is trustworthy. He has heard hadith from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him), while Salman Taymi and Muhammad bin Hujadah have narrated from him. Other than these two narrators, no one else has narrated from him. He is not a student of Kalbi, because the student of Kalbi is weak."
"5585","I did not see but good only (in my wife). Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Verily Allah has made her immune from all this. Then Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit and said: After this day no man should enter the house of another person in his absence, but only when he is accompanied by one person or two persons. (Using translation from Muslim 2173)"
"5586","Umar addressed the people in al­-Jabiyah, and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood as I am standing and said: ʿTreat my Companions kindly, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Then there will come people who will swear oaths before being asked to swear and will give testimony before being asked to give testimony. Whoever among you would like to attain the best place in Paradise, let him adhere to the jama'ah (the main body of Muslims), for the Shaitan is with one and he is further away from two. No man should be alone with a woman because the Shaitan will be the third one present. Whoever feels pleased when he does a good deed and feels bad when he does an evil deed is a believer.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 177)"
"5587","Behold, no person should spend the night with a married woman, but only in case he is married to her or he is her Mahram. (Using translation from Muslim 2171)"
"5588","Beware of getting, into the houses and meeting women (in seclusion). A person from the Ansar said: Messenger of Allah, what about husband's brother, whereupon he ﷺ said: Husband's brother is like death. (Using translation from Muslim 2172a)"
"5589","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) delivering a sermon on the pulpit, saying: ""No woman should ever travel without a mahram, and no man should be alone with a (non-mahram) woman unless her mahram is with her (then the ruling is different)."
"5590","Behold, no person should spend the night with a married woman, but only in case he is married to her or he is her Mahram. (Using translation from Muslim 2171)"
"5591","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while mentioning the world, said: The world is lush and sweet. You should try to avoid it, and especially be cautious regarding women. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned three women from the Children of Israel, two of whom were tall and one was short, who was not prominent. She had two wooden sandals made and a ring made in which the finest fragrance was filled. When she passed by the mosque (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) or by a group of people, she opened that ring, as a result of which its fragrance spread."
"5592","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""There was a woman from the Children of Israel who was short in stature. She had shoes made of wood, and when she walked between two tall women, she appeared tall because of them. She had a ring made of gold and filled its stone with the best musk fragrance. Whenever she passed by a gathering, she would shake that ring, as a result of which its fragrance would spread."
"5593","The narrator named Shareek states: If the navel were part of the private area, Sayyiduna Imam Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) would not have exposed it."
"5594","I have ten children. I have never kissed any of them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"5595","A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""You (people) kiss the boys! We don't kiss them."" The Prophet said, ""I cannot put mercy in your heart after Allah has taken it away from it."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5998)"
"5596","I did not expect that you would behave with him in this manner. By Allah! I also have a son but I have never kissed him.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
